<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The Windows installer people actually double-click.

  **Why there is a second Windows artifact.** The `.msi` is the install and has been since the first
  release, but a `.msi` is a Windows Installer database: double-clicking one is fine on a machine whose
  shell knows what to do with it, and it is the file people recognise as "the download". The `.exe` this
  file builds is a Burn bundle, a small native executable with the `.msi` inside it and a bootstrapper
  in front, which is what the rest of the world ships and what a reader opens without a second
  thought. The owner's instruction on 2026-09-30 was 需要一个单独的exe文件——也就是安装程序.

  **It is not a repackaging of the application.** The bundle carries the MSI and installs it; the MSI
  is still the thing that owns the files, the shortcuts and the uninstall entry. So there is exactly
  one description of what "installed" means, and the `.exe` is a delivery method rather than a second
  truth about the product.

  **Both are attached to the release, and neither replaces the other.** A reader who wants the MSI can
  still have it, which matters for the people who deploy software rather than run it.

  **The bundle's own version is the MSI's**, taken from the same expression the MSI's `Version` uses, so
  the two cannot disagree. WiX reads these comments as XML, where a doubled hyphen is not valid and
  is rejected as WIX0104 rather than repaired; write a comma or an em dash instead. Do not try to quote
  the forbidden character sequence here to warn about it, which is what this paragraph did first and
  why it failed its own check. `packaging/windows/check_comments.sh` enforces that for
  every file in this folder, and it caught exactly this mistake three times in one day.
-->
<Wix xmlns="http://wixtoolset.org/schemas/v4/wxs"
     xmlns:bal="http://wixtoolset.org/schemas/v4/wxs/bal">

  <Bundle
      Name="空庭 Hollow Court"
      Version="$(BundleVersion)"
      Manufacturer="S.M.Y.T."
      UpgradeCode="7F3A9C21-4E68-4B0D-9A52-1D8E6C4B7A33"
      IconSourceFile="$(BundleIcon)"
      AboutUrl="https://github.com/Nesarf/HollowCourt-Stable">

    <!--
      **The application's own icon, so the download looks like the application.** `BundleIcon` is the
      `.ico` Flutter already embeds, which is written by `art/render_icons.sh`, so the mark on the
      installer tracks the mark in the product rather than being a second drawing to keep in step.
    -->
    <!--
        **`hyperlinkLicense` with no license URL, and that is deliberate rather than an omission.** The
        stock bootstrapper's other themes show a "I accept the terms" checkbox, and there are no terms to
        accept: this is a per-user install of a cellar that lives in the reader's own documents folder,
        it asks for no elevation, and the project is public. A licence page with nothing on it is a
        click a reader has to make for no reason. `LicenseUrl=""` is what suppresses the link.
      -->
    <BootstrapperApplication>
      <bal:WixStandardBootstrapperApplication Theme="hyperlinkLicense" LicenseUrl="" />
    </BootstrapperApplication>

    <Chain>
      <!--
        **`Vital`, because there is nothing else in the chain to continue to.** A failed install has to
        be reported rather than skipped past.
      -->
      <MsiPackage SourceFile="$(MsiPath)" Vital="true" />
    </Chain>
  </Bundle>
</Wix>
